course: dictionary
lesson: 9378
title: Sporty: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «Growing, sporty children need regular meals» is about children who love sport, because children are people.
explain: «Sporty clothes» is different. Clothes cannot love sport, so here sporty means clothes that look like sports kit: casual and bright. Ask yourself: what is being described? A person, some clothes, or a car?
explain: Now look at «a sporty car». A car cannot play sport either, so sporty means fast and looking like a racing car. All three meanings link to sport, or to looking like sport.
fact: Sporty is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a person, clothes or a car.
fact: «Sporty» can mean a person who likes sport and is good at it, as in «the sporty type».
fact: «Sporty» can mean casual, bright clothes that look like sports clothes, as in «a sporty look».
fact: «Sporty» can mean fast and like a racing car, as in «a sporty car».
fact: Being sporty doesn't protect teeth: exercise uses energy, but sugar still feeds the germs that cause decay.
exercise: «Growing, sporty children need regular meals, and skipping meals leaves them tired and moody.» What does sporty mean in this sentence? | Fast, like a racing car | *Liking sport and being good at it | Very old | Bright and casual, like shop clothes
exercise: In a shop, Mia says, «That sporty jacket is bright and casual.» What does sporty mean here? | *Casual, bright clothes that look like sports clothes | A tall king | A person who loves football | A fast car
exercise: «He drove a sporty red car down the road.» What does sporty suggest? | A person who loves sport | Made of paper | Old and slow | *Fast and like a racing car
test: «Sporty clothes» is on the shop rail. Which meaning fits? | A fast car | A very old king | A person who likes sport | *Casual, bright clothes for sport
test: «A sporty car» is parked outside. Which meaning fits? | Happy to play football | Ancient and slow | *Fast, like a racing car | Casual clothes
exam: «Sporty kids don't need a special diet: the Eatwell Guide shows one plate for everybody.» What does this tell you? | *Sporty kids eat the same balanced plate as other children | Sporty means very old | Sporty kids never need fruit | Sporty kids need a different plate from everybody else
